            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0593" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/896c: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-14T15:00:00-05:00">November 14,
                            1941—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>268. The President today made a statement to the press that the Government of the
                    United States has decided to withdraw the American Marine detachments now
                    maintained ashore in China at Peiping, Tientsin, and Shanghai, and that it is
                    expected that the withdrawal will begin about November 25 and will be completed
                    shortly thereafter.</p>
                <pb facs="0594" n="584" xml:id="pg584"/>
                <p>Sent to Chungking. Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai, and Tientsin. Peiping repeat to
                    consular offices in Manchuria, including Dairen. Shanghai repeat to Hong Kong
                    and all consular offices in Japanese occupied China. Hong Kong repeat to Saigon
                    and Hanoi.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
